T-D46 evidence hook -- the TEMPORARY patch that makes the on-machine scene possible.
===============================================================================

WHY IT EXISTS
-------------
Two things the shipped client cannot do, both of them scene set-up rather than
logic under test:

  * F7/F8 summon a Hollow Wretch 2 blocks in front of the player (F7 straight
    ahead, F8 ahead and one block to the right). Hostile mobs only spawn where
    the effective light is 0 (docs/01 §6) and this world has no day/night cycle,
    so the lit surface can never produce one. This is the SAME hook T-M2 used for
    its own on-machine evidence (docs/qa/T-M2-2026-09-18/tools/tm2_evidence_hook.patch);
  * F9/F10 wear / take off the four timber_* armour pieces. T-D46 gave those four
    items the leather-tier numbers, but the shipped client has NO WAY to put an
    item into an armour cell: the four cells (36..39) are only ever written by
    Inventory::set_slot, and the client never calls it for them (no equip key, no
    inventory screen - the E-screen is a later card). Reported in
    docs/tasks/T-D46.report.md §"需 PM 裁决项".

F9/F10 write the armour cells DIRECTLY through the inventory the tick already
reads, so the damage reduction measured on-machine is the shipped
player_life.hpp code path; nothing in tick.cpp / player_life.hpp /
world_sim.cpp / mob_sim.hpp is touched by this patch.

WHAT IT DOES NOT DO
-------------------
It does not touch the combat rules, the damage entry, the armour formula, the
hurt window or the knockback. Every number in the captured log is produced by the
delivered sources.

